ed by projected DraftKings points. Pts/$1K is projected points per $1,000 of salary.</p>\n<p>VIP members get SPAGS projections, exports and simulation results for every player in the Splash Play NBA tool. <a href=\"/nba/\">Open the NBA DFS tool →</a></p>\n<h2>How to use the rankings</h2>\n<p>A ranking by projection shows who should score the most, not who fits a lineup. Use the Pts/$1K column to see what each player returns for his price, and check each player's status before the first game.</p>\n<h2>More for this slate</h2>\n<p><a href=\"/dfs/nba/today/\">Picks and projections</a> · <a href=\"/dfs/nba/projections/\">Projections</a> · <a href=\"/dfs/nba/value-plays/\">Value plays</a></p>\n<h2>NBA DFS rankings FAQ for Nov 11</h2>\n<h3>Who is the top-ranked NBA DFS player for Wednesday, November 11?</h3>\n<p>Nikola Jokic (DEN) leads the SPAGS model at 62.1 projected DraftKings points for $11,500 on the main slate, as of November 11, 11:53 AM ET.</p>\n<h3>How many players are ranked?</h3>\n<p>100 players on the 7-games DraftKings main slate, ranked by SPAGS projection.</p>\n<h3>Where can I get DraftKings NBA DFS projections and simulations?</h3>\n<p>Splash Play, built by Chris Spags, offers DraftKings NBA DFS projections, exports and simulation results. These pages show free SPAGS projections for the DraftKings main slate. Squirt Squad covers matchup research and the Projection Matrix. VIP adds SPAGS projections, exports and simulation results. Simulations are modeled outcomes, not guaranteed results. <a data-slate-join href=\"/join/\">Compare Splash Play plans →</a></p>\n<h3>How are these NBA DFS projections made?</h3>\n<p>They are SPAGS projections from the Splash Play NBA model, built by Chris Spags, in DraftKings scoring.</p>\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Who is the top-ranked NBA DFS player for Wednesday, November 11?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\